Only fail a streamed response when n8n sent nothing but errors.

Upstream raises HomeAssistantError on the first {"type": "error"} chunk. n8n's
streaming webhook also emits error chunks for failures the AI Agent recovers
from: a tool call that returns HTTP 400 and is retried, or a model call that is
rate limited and covered by the fallback model. Home Assistant then drops the
reply even though the workflow finishes with a good answer. Seen with the Home
Metrics Agent: HA reported a VictoriaMetrics query error at 7.4 s while the
execution went on to answer at 10.7 s with status success.

With this patch, error chunks are logged at warning level and skipped. The
request fails only if the stream closes without any item or tool_calls chunk,
and then it fails with the last error message, as upstream would have.

Revisit on every version bump: drop this patch if upstream stops treating every
error chunk as fatal.

diff --git a/custom_components/webhook_conversation/entity.py b/custom_components/webhook_conversation/entity.py
index b63a881..3f22596 100644
--- a/custom_components/webhook_conversation/entity.py
+++ b/custom_components/webhook_conversation/entity.py
@@ -157,6 +157,8 @@ class WebhookConversationLLMBaseEntity(WebhookConversationBaseEntity):
                     f"Error contacting webhook: HTTP {response.status} - {response.reason}"
                 )
 
+            last_error: Any = None
+            has_content = False
             async for line in response.content:
                 if line:
                     line_str = line.decode("utf-8").strip()
@@ -165,9 +167,19 @@ class WebhookConversationLLMBaseEntity(WebhookConversationBaseEntity):
                             chunk_data = json.loads(line_str)
                             chunk_type = chunk_data.get("type")
                             if chunk_type == "error":
-                                raise HomeAssistantError(
-                                    f"n8n error: {chunk_data.get('message', chunk_data)}"
+                                # n8n also emits error chunks for failures the
+                                # agent recovers from (a tool call it retries, a
+                                # model error covered by the fallback model), so
+                                # only fail if the stream produced nothing else.
+                                last_error = chunk_data.get(
+                                    "message", chunk_data.get("content", chunk_data)
                                 )
+                                _LOGGER.warning(
+                                    "Webhook streamed an error chunk: %s", last_error
+                                )
+                                continue
+                            if chunk_type in ("item", "tool_calls"):
+                                has_content = True
                             # We don't break on "end" because n8n can send multiple
                             # begin/end blocks when using tools or intermediate steps.
                             # We keep reading until the stream actually closes.
@@ -177,6 +189,8 @@ class WebhookConversationLLMBaseEntity(WebhookConversationBaseEntity):
                                 "Failed to parse streaming response chunk: %s", line_str
                             )
                             continue
+            if not has_content and last_error is not None:
+                raise HomeAssistantError(f"n8n error: {last_error}")
 
     def _build_payload(
         self, chat_log: conversation.ChatLog, include_last: bool = False
